# Copy this file to .leakwords.local (git-ignored, never pushed) and list the names that
# must not leave the repository: your company, project prefixes, bastion hosts,
# namespaces, internal domains…
#
# One extended regular expression (ERE) per line. Blank lines and lines starting with #
# are ignored. tools/check-leaks.sh looks for them in the working tree and in the whole
# git history.
#
# The reason this list lives outside the repo is simple: if the names were in a public
# file, that file would be the leak.
#
# Examples of what is worth listing:
#
# mycompany
# my-project-prefix-
# internal-bastion
# my-cluster-name
# intranet\.mycompany\.com
